# Secrets. backend/.env holds SECRET_KEY, the SQLite path, OAuth client
# secrets for Microsoft/QuickBooks/Xero, the Xero webhook key and the Paddle
# credentials. The .example files are templates and ARE committed - that is how
# a new developer learns which settings exist. Hence the explicit negation.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
# Templates that are not named exactly `.env.example`. Without this,
# deploy/.env.production.example matched `.env.*` above and was dropped from the
# deploy commit - `git add` skips ignored files without a word, so the file
# existed on disk and was named in the instructions, but was absent from every
# clone. `cp deploy/.env.production.example .env` then failed on a fresh server.
# Broad on purpose: anything ending `.example` is a template by definition.
!*.example

# Local database. Never commit: it contains every employee, payslip and
# subscription row in the dev database.
*.sqlite3
*.sqlite3-journal
*.db

# User uploads. backend/media currently holds real employee documents and CSV
# exports; MEDIA_ROOT is created on demand by Django's storage backend, so
# ignoring the whole directory is safe.
backend/media/

# Build output.
# backend/frontend_dist is generated by `npm run build` in frontend/ and served
# as STATICFILES_DIRS. It is derived from frontend/src, so committing it makes
# every diff unreadable and lets stale bundles be deployed. Rebuild it instead.
backend/frontend_dist/
backend/staticfiles/

# Dependencies.
frontend/node_modules/
package-lock.json.bak

# Vercel local build/link state. `vercel dev -L` writes one per service root
# (so backend/.vercel/ as well as .vercel/), and it records the linked project
# id and dev-server settings. Not build output - regenerable, but it is per
# machine and was previously untracked-and-unignored.
.vercel/

# Python bytecode and virtualenvs.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/

# Test / tooling caches.
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
coverage/

# Editor and OS noise.
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini